              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lilcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You had me at \"tomato\" and \"rosemary\". I made this as written and will make often as it is easy to prepare. I may cut back on the oil next time to make it lower still in fat than it already is. Thank you for this!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joanne Hoschette"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have not tried this with RICE WINE vinegar yet. However it is great with red wine vinegar. Sometimes I add in 1t. to 2t. of balsamic. I also like it with small mozzerella balls &amp; fresh torn basil. IF there are any left overs, remove mozzerella , then pulse briefly to make a fresh salad dressing. During the winter months , when fresh tomatoes are all hot house grown, I find that grape tomatoes are a good substitute.",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-30T04:06:56.337Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elise"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty! I will use less olive oil to cut the calories when I make it again. Also, I made a couple of other tomato salad recipes this summer, and learned that the letting the salad sit for a couple of hours allows the tomatoes to marinate in the sauce and absorb the flavors. We served this when we had friends over for dinner and our guests went back for seconds. Very tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-09T04:42:37.037Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lisam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had to add 1 tbls white balsamic\nand 1 tbs red wine vinegar\ntouch of thyme sea salt to give it a little zing. I did add thinly sliced red onion. For leftover tomato salad, I added arugula the second day and it was great!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-25T18:18:32.883Z"
          },
          {
